Z||000000||mbramble||08-22-2000||07:55 AM||||Have been holding off on getting new tires until I got the Tech wheels I bought stripped, polished and painted.  Pretty much done but for some additional polishing when one of the local tire stores had a great deal on tires (standard 185 75R14).  So, I took the wheels down, asked them to check shocks, struts, do a 4 wheel alignment and put the new tires on my Tech wheels.  <P>Shocks and struts were in good shape but the he said the rear alignment was way off.  Must be the reason the tires were wearing funny back there.  And, I had a real bad shake at 63-68 MPH.  Real bad!!<P>After the work was done, drove up the highway to drop the car back off at my son's high school (he's driving it these days).  Hit 75 3 different times and no shake at all!  Runs the same at 65 as it does at 25.  It's like a new car!!  <P>Wish I had gotten the 4 wheel alignment done sooner (it was only $49.00).<P>And my wheels -- painted the same maroon as the car where the black used to be, and polished everywhere else -- look good.  Will post some pics soon...<BR>||||reg||1
